hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16761","He said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abbad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from a man from Banu Salit, that he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting at the door of his mosque leaning, with a Qitri garment upon him and no other garment upon him, saying: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor forsake him; then he pointed with his hand to his chest saying: Taqwa is here, taqwa is here."
